WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
(audience applauds)
- So I'm such a fan.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.400
You look gorgeous.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.657
I've been a fan since like,

00:00:03.657 --> 00:00:04.620
you probably hate this.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.970
It's like everybody sings
"Since You've Been Gone" to me.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.340
But like Percy Jackson days,
like, I have loved you since.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.270
- I love that.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.103
- Okay. Okay.

00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:13.200
- No, I love that people
still love Percy Jackson.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.820
- Yeah. Well I also have kids now too

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.920
so now we're like revamping it all.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.300
But last year you got married, right?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.133
- Yes.
- Yes!

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.270
Did everything go as
planned or was anything.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.830
- Yeah, I mean most of it went as planned.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.990
I tried to, you know, we
did the best we could.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.243
We had a wedding planner,
but you know, like life.

00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:28.140
- Yep.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.830
- Things happen and you have
to sort of go with the flow.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.663
- Yeah.

00:00:32.663 --> 00:00:34.200
- I mean there was an
issue with the bus that was

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.960
supposed to take everyone
from the hotel to the venue

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.730
which was less than a mile, by the way.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.720
So they could have walked and

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.010
it would've been less problematic,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.210
but it hit a curb, then hit another curb.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.043
- What?

00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:46.876
- Got lost.

00:00:46.876 --> 00:00:47.709
- Was everyone Okay?

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:48.542
- Got lost and it was a mile away.

00:00:48.542 --> 00:00:50.400
- And then tried to drop everyone off

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.900
in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.270
- Was the driver inebriated? (laughs)

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.250
- No.
- Like, I was like , wait.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.680
- No, I think maybe there was a wrong.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.210
- Miscommunication.
- Yes.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.640
- I don't wanna throw
anyone under the bus,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.473
so to speak.

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.340
- Yeah, on TV.
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.173
- That's right.

00:01:06.173 --> 00:01:09.273
But it was, it ended up being fine but,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.880
no one really wanted to bring it up to me.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.980
But then of course my best
friend was like, "Oh my God

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.813
it was a disaster."

00:01:14.813 --> 00:01:15.646
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:01:15.646 --> 00:01:18.037
- We were all on the side of
the road and we were like,

00:01:18.037 --> 00:01:19.950
"We don't think this is it."

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.682
But then you just sort
of go with the flow and,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.515
not take it too seriously.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:26.267
- It looked magical, I saw the
pictures, it looked magical.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.440
And that flower thing behind you.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.060
The wall of beauty.
- Beautiful.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.470
- Yeah, and that's so cute.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.300
You're such a handsome couple anyway.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.133
- Yeah.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.400
- So what do you plan to do, this year,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.990
to take care of yourself
maybe just a little better?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.823
Do better at?

00:01:38.687 --> 00:01:41.700
- I mean, I always, I'm
obsessed with acupuncture.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.870
I do that a ton.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.460
- I love acupuncture.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.260
- To the point where I probably should

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.767
have, like, an affair with an
acupuncturist to save money.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.700
- 'Cause you spend so much money. (laughs)

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.858
- That's right.
- I used to make fun of it.

00:01:52.858 --> 00:01:53.850
I dunno how my husband would feel about.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.170
- No, but I used to make fun of it.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.510
But it really, it truly, like, healed.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.980
This thing I had going on with my foot.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.180
They said I was gonna have to have surgery

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.110
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.520
And then like all of a sudden it healed.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.420
It's real.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.253
It's true.

00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:05.227
- It is.
- Yes.

00:02:05.227 --> 00:02:07.710
- And I, go sometimes
three, four times a week.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.820
Which is so.
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.653
- It's my addiction.

00:02:09.653 --> 00:02:11.160
- It does make you feel really good.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:11.993
- Yes.

00:02:11.993 --> 00:02:13.440
- It is a certain kind
of high, I will say that.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.273
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:15.106
- And I think it's a good opportunity.

00:02:15.106 --> 00:02:15.939
- It's a healthy addiction.

00:02:15.939 --> 00:02:18.000
- Yeah, I mean, if you're
constantly on your phone

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.710
and you have so much going on and even

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.530
if it's just an opportunity
to lie there and,

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.247
sort of meditate or do nothing
and just be by yourself.

00:02:26.247 --> 00:02:27.570
So, that's nice.
- You have to nothing.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:28.563
There's a bunch of needles in you.

00:02:28.563 --> 00:02:29.610
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.170
- Yes, exactly.
You can't move.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.550
- Yeah, I'm with you on that.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.950
Okay, so I'm told you
recently went, is it to Paris?

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.150
- [Kelly] Is that where you were?

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:36.983
- [Alexandra] Yes.

00:02:36.983 --> 00:02:38.070
- [Kelly] I love Paris.
Did you love it?

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.330
- I love Paris.
- Yeah.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.800
I will, say I'm not, you know
how everybody's like, "Paris."

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.260
I'm not that about it, but I liked it.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.340
I thought it was cool.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.740
- Well, the Eiffel Tower
- It's beautiful.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.210
- I mean if you like go.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.100
- I just think everybody sets it up.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.540
- Well, there's a problem, right?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.490
When you set something up to be like.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.323
- Yeah.

00:02:57.323 --> 00:02:58.600
When everyone says, "Oh
my God, you have to go."

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.690
"It's the most amazing place on Earth."

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.070
And then you have, I don't know what.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.500
You have these expectations
that it's gonna be.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.610
- Yeah.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.080
- And then it's just a city I guess.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:07.913
- I know!

00:03:07.913 --> 00:03:09.487
And then I'm like, Paris is amazing.

00:03:09.487 --> 00:03:10.320
- A great city.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.190
- By the way, Paris is amazing.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.230
But so is the rest of France.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.140
Like, the rest of France is beautiful.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.250
- Well, the south of France
is, France is beautiful.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.083
Yeah.

00:03:18.083 --> 00:03:18.916
- Europe in general is gorgeous.

00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:20.880
- Yeah, were you working
or was it for play?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.930
- Little bit of both.
- Oh, okay.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.850
- I go do the fashion stuff.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:24.839
- Oh, okay.
- Yes.

00:03:24.839 --> 00:03:27.600
So have you ever had any
big fails while traveling?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.920
'Cause you like to travel.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:29.753
- I love to travel.

00:03:29.753 --> 00:03:31.230
Yeah, I've been really lucky.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.190
I mean, when I was younger, I
don't do it now as much, but

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.960
I used to just sort of,
when I was in Europe,

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.723
jump on the train and and go.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.020
I would just go and see what I could

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:43.931
find out in the country.

00:03:43.931 --> 00:03:44.764
- That's fun.

00:03:44.764 --> 00:03:46.620
I was in Germany once
and I was in Berlin and

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.620
I jumped on the train and I
went out to the countryside

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.750
and I got lost.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.210
But I was somewhere where
no one spoke English and

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.500
I do not speak German.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.720
And so then I started to sort of panic and

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.580
I was young enough that I couldn't really

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.350
control my emotions.
- Yeah.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.970
- And I just start sobbing.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.190
And these, like, very nice people were

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:11.280
speaking to me in German,
like, "Are you okay?"

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.530
And we couldn't communicate.
- Sad little American girl.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.330
- Yeah, it was very embarrassing.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.040
And I had to pull myself together and

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.300
finally I found the right train.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.560
But it was like this,

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.020
you know when you're traveling
you get overwhelmed and you.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.348
- Yeah.

00:04:23.348 --> 00:04:25.650
- But, but going alone and
traveling like that is cool.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.483
That's brave.

00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:27.720
- Yeah, it's very cool, yeah.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.360
Except the people thought
I was a complete weirdo.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.360
I was being very dramatic
over probably nothing.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.700
- No, I would've gotten scared, I would.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.206
I believe in the buddy system though.

00:04:37.206 --> 00:04:38.039
- I was somehow scared for no reason.

00:04:38.039 --> 00:04:40.140
- I saw too many "Dateline" specials.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.266
I believe in a buddy system. (laughs)

00:04:41.266 --> 00:04:42.099
(audience laughs)

00:04:42.099 --> 00:04:44.715
If I'm going down, I'm taking
a buddy with me. (laughs)

00:04:44.715 --> 00:04:46.200
(audience laughs)
It's like, that's my system.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.690
So your new show is
called "Mayfair Witches."

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.190
So could you tell us a little about it?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.510
- It's about a girl.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:55.170
She's a doctor surgeon and she finds out

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.340
that she is a witch.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.020
And that she belongs
to a different family.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.025
She was adopted and she
finds out that she's actually

00:05:01.025 --> 00:05:04.410
part of this family
called the, the Mayfairs.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:08.220
And it's quite amazing
to do a role like this

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.410
'cause it really is sort
of a metaphor for life.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.360
Like when you're going
through huge transitions

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.680
how do you handle it?
- Yeah.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.020
- Only this person's
transition is, you know,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.370
that she has these powers.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.203
And how do you control them and all that.

00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:19.178
- Which is fun.

00:05:19.178 --> 00:05:20.011
- It's great fun.

00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:21.120
I love that kind of escapism.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.069
- Yeah.
- That's fun.

00:05:22.069 --> 00:05:22.902
- Yeah.

00:05:22.902 --> 00:05:25.440
So ever experienced anything
supernatural like in your life?

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.850
- I haven't personally.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.627
I do think there's some
things that are like,

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.540
"Is that a coincidence or how did that?"

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.333
There's a lot of magic
in the world in that way.

00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:33.166
- Yeah.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.710
But there was one time
I was shooting a film

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.070
in Louisiana and I was in a little town

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.440
outside of place called Shreveport.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.560
And one of the members of
the crew, a girl, starts

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.540
crying outside of the
house we were shooting in.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.687
And she said, "I can't."

00:05:46.687 --> 00:05:47.947
"I can't go in there."

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.830
"There's a woman in the corner of the room

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:54.607
saying, 'What are you
all doing in my house?'"

00:05:54.607 --> 00:05:56.190
"Get out of my house."

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.660
And she said, "I can't go in there."

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.770
And she wouldn't come into work.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.610
And then later that day we
all found out the husband,

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.997
the owner of the house said,

00:06:03.997 --> 00:06:06.184
"My wife passed away in that room."

00:06:06.184 --> 00:06:07.017
- What?

00:06:07.017 --> 00:06:09.300
- And there was no way
for her to know about it.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.330
But I didn't see the ghost.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.650
- Oh, lucky.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.320
- But that always creeps
me out 'cause I've never

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.120
found an explanation for it.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:20.010
- Yeah, no, I don't wanna, I always,

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.127
I just speak out like,

00:06:21.127 --> 00:06:23.097
"Please don't show yourself
to me 'cause I will die."

00:06:23.097 --> 00:06:23.930
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.044
- Yeah, I think it's.
- I'll join you. (laughs)

00:06:27.044 --> 00:06:28.470
- All the ghosts are being nice to us.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.303
They're like, they can't handle it.

00:06:29.303 --> 00:06:31.110
- Yeah, just live your life wherever I am.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.280
Fine, don't show me you.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.390
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.346
Congrats though on everything.
- Thank you.

00:06:35.346 --> 00:06:38.100
- I literally, I was late to the game on

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.290
getting to watch "White Lotus."

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.200
Congrats on it because
I, literally, got sick

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.490
for like three weeks, it felt like.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.487
And I was like, "Oh my God."

00:06:45.487 --> 00:06:46.710
"I've never gotten to
watch this whole thing."

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.170
I watched the whole thing
like back to back to back.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.420
It was so good, so talented.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.120
Do you feel like, 'cause
I've known you for a while,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.560
I feel like, since you were little,

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.940
and so I've been watching
you for a minute.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.040
But some people are like,
"Oh my God, she's amazing."

00:06:59.040 --> 00:06:59.886
And just discovering you.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:04.260
Do you feel like it's been a
long road to have that moment?

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.610
Like a "White Lotus" moment?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.020
- Yeah, I mean, I think I've had

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.240
a lot of ups and downs in
my career, like anyone.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.700
I mean, this career is you've probably.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.860
- Oh, music.
- I mean, you're amazing.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.254
- Oh no, I think every
career has ebbs and flows.

00:07:15.254 --> 00:07:17.520
- And yeah, it's a little
bit of ups and downs and

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.380
so I feel, in a way, like I've been

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.360
discovered over and over and over.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.614
- It's kind of cool
- Sort of.

00:07:22.614 --> 00:07:25.710
But, there's always that, and I think,

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:29.290
with the Emmy nomination
with "White Lotus," you know

00:07:30.313 --> 00:07:32.610
it's sort of like
overnight being discovered.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.443
- But you've been doing it forever, yeah.

00:07:33.443 --> 00:07:34.276
But you've been doing it for 20 years.

00:07:34.276 --> 00:07:37.290
So I just think it's about
doing what you love and

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.700
doing it for the right reasons.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.600
And, and then, you know,
hopefully it all works out.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.240
But it's been really special for me.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.320
I feel really lucky.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.330
- Yeah, it is funny though
when you said, sort of.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.640
I was like, yeah, that's kind
of like when I go somewhere

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:51.487
and I sing somewhere and they're like,

00:07:51.487 --> 00:07:52.950
"Oh my, you're a good singer."

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.310
And I'm like, "Ah, okay."
(audience laughs)

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.248
(Alexandra laughs)

00:07:56.248 --> 00:07:58.470
- Like, it's been a minute, but all right.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.303
- Yeah.

00:07:59.303 --> 00:08:00.136
- Yeah, or they're like, "Oh
wow, Alex is a good actress?"

00:08:00.136 --> 00:08:01.647
- Or like, "Do you have an a record?"

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.480
"Do you have a record?"

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.460
And I'm like, well, and
then, like, alright. (laughs)

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.690
But it's like, it's one
of those things where

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:07.980
you do, you feel like you've been working,

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.560
but sometimes people do,
they're just discovering you.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.970
For whatever reason they
haven't seen, or whatever,

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:12.870
or heard or whatever.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.220
- Yeah.
It is kind of cool though.

